# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots php-fpm AND nginx with the vulnerable php.ini
# (disable_functions empty, allow_url_include=On, expose_php=On) and then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * both daemons are ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what
#     makes the "fixed the config but never restarted the service" case
#     detectable - php-fpm keeps its old php.ini in memory, so the
#     X-Powered-By header survives a file-only edit;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting php-fpm or nginx cannot
#     kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART php-fpm, not merely start it if
# absent - the pool is already up with the vulnerable configuration.
